\title{Triangular numbers}
\date{2026-03-14T14:04:46Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

##{0, 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, \dots}

\p{These are the \em{triangular numbers}, because #{a_n} is the number of dots in an equilateral triangle with #{n} dots on a side.}

\p{Notice how the gap between successive terms increases by #{1} every time. This satisfies the recurrence

##{\begin{align*}
    \triangle_0 &= 0 \\
    \triangle_n &= \triangle_{n-1} + n
\end{align*}}

There is also a closed form for #{\triangle_n} which we’ll derive shortly.}
